    "place_value_basics": {
      "id": "place_value_basics",
      "type": "CONTENT",
      "content": {
        "text": "Let's build the idea from the right side.\n\nTake:\n\n57,348\n\nRead the positions from right to left:\n\n8 → ones\n4 → tens\n3 → hundreds\n7 → thousands\n5 → ten-thousands\n\nSo every step to the left multiplies the place by 10.\n\nThat gives us:\n\n8 × 1 = 8\n4 × 10 = 40\n3 × 100 = 300\n7 × 1,000 = 7,000\n5 × 10,000 = 50,000\n\nThis is positional notation: the value of a digit depends on where it is placed.",
        "avatarPersona": "TUTOR"
      },
      "transitions": [
        {
          "targetNodeId": "place_value_check"
        }
      ]
    },
    "place_value_deeper": {
      "id": "place_value_deeper",
      "type": "CONTENT",
      "content": {
        "text": "Now compare two terms that students often mix up:\n\nFace value\nPlace value\n\nFace value is simply the digit itself.\n\nIn 57,348:\nthe face value of 7 is 7.\n\nIts place value is 7,000 because it sits in the thousands place.\n\nSo:\n\nFace value → what digit do I see?\nPlace value → what is that digit worth in its position?\n\nThis distinction is very important because aptitude questions may ask for either one.",
        "avatarPersona": "TUTOR"
      },
      "transitions": [
        {
          "targetNodeId": "face_value_check"
        }
      ]
    },
    "place_value_remedy": {
      "id": "place_value_remedy",
      "type": "CONTENT",
      "content": {
        "text": "Let's slow it down.\n\nFor 57,348, count from the right:\n\n8 → ones\n4 → tens\n3 → hundreds\n7 → thousands\n\nSo the 7 represents seven thousands:\n\n7 × 1,000 = 7,000\n\nRemember: place value is not just the digit.\nIt is:\n\ndigit × value of its position.\n\nTry a similar one now.",
        "avatarPersona": "TUTOR"
      },
      "transitions": [
        {
          "targetNodeId": "place_value_retry"
        }
      ]
    },
