    "expanded_form_remedy": {
      "id": "expanded_form_remedy",
      "type": "CONTENT",
      "content": {
        "text": "Let's place every digit carefully.\n\nFor 6,042:\n\n2 → ones = 2\n4 → tens = 40\n0 → hundreds = 0\n6 → thousands = 6,000\n\nTherefore:\n\n6,042 = 6,000 + 40 + 2\n\nThe zero is important because it holds the hundreds position even though it contributes no value.",
        "avatarPersona": "TUTOR"
      },
