    "smallest_number_remedy": {
      "id": "smallest_number_remedy",
      "type": "CONTENT",
      "content": {
        "text": "This is the important exception.\n\nTo make the smallest 4-digit number from 0, 2, 5 and 7, we cannot start with 0.\n\nSo start with the smallest non-zero digit:\n\n2\n\nThen use the smallest remaining digit:\n\n0\n\nThen arrange what is left in ascending order:\n\n5, 7\n\nResult:\n\n2,057\n\nThe trick is:\n\nsmallest non-zero first → zero next → rest ascending.",
        "avatarPersona": "TUTOR"
      },
      "transitions": [
        {
          "targetNodeId": "smallest_number_retry"
        }
      ]
    },
    "number_formation_remedy": {
      "id": "number_formation_remedy",
      "type": "CONTENT",
      "content": {
        "text": "Build the number from its place values:\n\n3 thousands = 3,000\n6 hundreds = 600\n0 tens = 0\n4 ones = 4\n\nNow add them:\n\n3,000 + 600 + 0 + 4 = 3,604\n\nSo the number is 3,604.\n\nThe same positional idea works in both directions:\nwe can break a number apart, or build a number from its parts.",
        "avatarPersona": "TUTOR"
      },
      "transitions": [
        {
          "targetNodeId": "number_formation_retry"
        }
      ]
